1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Level one, the seminarian.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:07,120
You were 18 years old. You grew up in a

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,960
village high in the mountains. The

4
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:10,160
church bell measured every day of your

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:11,720
life.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,080
Your mother took you to mass before you

7
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,840
could walk. She prayed the rosary every

8
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,880
night by candlelight.

9
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:18,960
Your father said little and prayed even

10
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:20,640
less.

11
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:22,560
He worked the fields until his back

12
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,960
finally gave out.

13
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:28,720
You have one younger sister named Maria.

14
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:30,360
She is 14 and she thinks you are crazy.

15
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,920
You served as an altar boy from the age

16
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:35,440
of seven. You loved the smell of incense

17
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:37,040
and the quiet of the empty church.

18
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:38,440
One morning you felt something you could

19
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:40,320
not explain.

20
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:42,040
You called it a calling because you had

21
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,640
no other word.

22
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:46,680
You told your mother first. She wept and

23
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:49,080
held your face in her hands.

24
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:51,160
You told the parish priest next.

25
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:52,480
He smiled like he had been waiting years

26
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,200
for this.

27
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:55,360
He wrote a letter to the diocese on your

28
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,320
behalf.

29
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:58,480
Now you stand at the gate of a seminary

30
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:00,720
in the city.

31
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:02,760
You carry one suitcase and a Bible your

32
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:04,519
grandmother left you.

33
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,760
The building is old and gray and

34
00:01:04,519 --> 00:01:07,600
enormous.

35
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:10,120
Other young men arrive on the same gray

36
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:11,920
morning. They look as nervous as you

37
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:13,560
feel inside.

38
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:16,280
You were assigned a small room with a

39
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:18,440
bed, a desk, and a crucifix.

40
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:21,080
There is no decoration on the walls.

41
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:23,280
There is no comfort anywhere.

42
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:25,000
The day begins at 5:00 in the morning.

43
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:26,080
You rise in the dark and walk to the

44
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,680
chapel.

45
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,760
You pray before the sun is even up.

46
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:32,880
You study Latin, philosophy, and

47
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,200
theology for hours.

48
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,640
You learn the history of the church

49
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,680
going back 2,000 years.

50
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:40,440
You learn that faith is not a feeling

51
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:42,920
but a discipline.

52
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:45,080
The professors are demanding and cold.

53
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:47,200
The schedule is brutal.

54
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:48,480
You scrub floors and wash dishes like

55
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:50,600
everyone else.

56
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:52,400
You are tested constantly, though not

57
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:54,040
always with exams.

58
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,320
They are watching to see if your calling

59
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:58,040
is real.

60
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:00,360
Some men leave after only a month. They

61
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,800
miss women, freedom, or the lives they

62
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:04,240
left behind.

63
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:07,080
Nobody shames them for walking away. The

64
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:08,560
priesthood is not made for everyone.

65
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:10,080
You miss your mother.

66
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:12,320
You miss her cooking.

67
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:13,720
The food is cold. You eat among

68
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:16,320
strangers.

69
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:19,320
A bell rules you again. A louder bell

70
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:22,160
this time. Lights out at 10:00.

71
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:23,400
You stare at the crucifix. You ask God a

72
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:25,680
question.

73
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:28,320
He answers in silence.

74
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:30,120
The silence brings a strange peace. You

75
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:32,080
confess your doubts.

76
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:35,000
A director hears them all.

77
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:36,040
Doubt is not the enemy. Pride is the

78
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,760
enemy.

79
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:42,320
You write it down. You read it often.

80
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:45,200
The hard days come. The calling holds

81
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:47,480
you. It will not let go.

82
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:49,640
You belong to God now.

83
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,880
You stay because the quiet voice has not

84
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,480
stopped.

85
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:55,160
You write letters home that your mother

86
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:57,680
reads aloud to the whole village.

87
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:59,519
Level two, the deacon.

88
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,920
Six years have passed since you walked

89
00:02:59,519 --> 00:03:02,880
through that gate.

90
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:04,600
You survived the seminary when half your

91
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:06,320
class did not.

92
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,840
The bishop laid his hands on your head

93
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:09,959
in the cathedral.

94
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:11,400
Your mother sat in the front row weeping

95
00:03:09,959 --> 00:03:14,560
with joy.

96
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:16,440
Maria came, too. Now 20 and engaged to a

97
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:18,959
young mechanic.

98
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:20,519
You are now a transitional deacon.

99
00:03:18,959 --> 00:03:22,480
This is the final step before the

100
00:03:20,519 --> 00:03:24,480
priesthood itself.

101
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:26,040
You wear the stole across one shoulder

102
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,120
like a sash.

103
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:30,040
You can preach the gospel. You can

104
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:31,880
baptize the newborn.

105
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,239
You can witness marriages and conduct

106
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:35,280
funerals.

107
00:03:33,239 --> 00:03:37,280
You cannot yet say mass or hear

108
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:38,760
confessions.

109
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,680
You are assigned to a parish in a

110
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:43,560
working-class town.

111
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:45,200
The pastor is old and tired and grateful

112
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:47,400
for the help.

113
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:49,200
You visit the sick in their homes.

114
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,519
You sit with the dying and hold their

115
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:52,800
hands.

116
00:03:50,519 --> 00:03:54,600
You bury the dead and comfort families

117
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:56,120
left behind.

118
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,520
You learn that ministry is not

119
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:59,600
glamorous.

120
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,920
It is mostly showing up when nobody else

121
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:02,600
will.

122
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:05,160
You teach catechism to children who

123
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:07,400
would rather be anywhere else.

124
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:10,040
You read the gospel at mass and feel the

125
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:11,640
weight of every word.

126
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:13,480
You make mistakes.

127
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:15,120
You stumble over Latin you thought you

128
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:17,239
had mastered.

129
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:19,120
The old pastor corrects you gently and

130
00:04:17,239 --> 00:04:22,440
tells you stories.

131
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:24,440
He has been a priest for 40 long years.

132
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:26,240
He warns you that the collar changes how

133
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,919
people see you.

134
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:29,919
Some will trust you with secrets they

135
00:04:27,919 --> 00:04:31,880
tell no one else.

136
00:04:29,919 --> 00:04:33,720
Some will resent you for what they think

137
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:35,960
you represent.

138
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:38,280
You take a vow of celibacy you do not

139
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:40,480
yet fully understand.

140
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:42,280
You promise obedience to your bishop and

141
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:44,320
his successors.

142
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:46,040
You give up the family you might one day

143
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:47,640
have had.

144
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:49,360
You tell yourself that the church is

145
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:51,400
your family now.

146
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:53,760
You wear black now.

147
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:56,240
Children stare on the street.

148
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:58,800
Old women bless themselves.

149
00:04:56,240 --> 00:05:01,280
You are a symbol to them.

150
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:03,520
The weight feels strange.

151
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:05,360
You preach your first homily.

152
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:07,640
Your hands sweat.

153
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:09,640
Your voice cracks once.

154
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:12,120
Then it studies.

155
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:14,480
The words come on their own.

156
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:17,720
A woman says it moved her.

157
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:20,000
You hold those words for weeks.

158
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:21,919
You learn the poor by name.

159
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,440
You bring them bread.

160
00:05:21,919 --> 00:05:26,720
Maria sends a wedding invitation.

161
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:29,280
You cannot give her away.

162
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:31,960
You bless her marriage instead.

163
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:34,800
You return to the rectory alone.

164
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:36,640
The church is family now.

165
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,440
Late at night, you wonder if that will

166
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:40,840
ever be enough.

167
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:42,600
You push the thought down and return to

168
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:45,600
your prayers.

169
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:48,080
Level three, the parish priest.

170
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:49,880
The day you waited for finally arrives.

171
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:51,200
The bishop ordains you a priest of the

172
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:53,280
diocese.

173
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:55,040
You lie face down on the cold cathedral

174
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:56,960
floor during the litany.

175
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:58,600
When you rise, you are something you can

176
00:05:56,960 --> 00:06:00,920
never stop being.

177
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:02,680
The change is permanent, and you feel it

178
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:04,520
in your bones.

179
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:05,520
You say your first mass the very next

180
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,360
morning.

181
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:08,760
Your hands shake as you lift the host

182
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:10,400
above the altar.

183
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:13,720
Your mother receives communion from her

184
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:15,280
own son and cannot stop crying.

185
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,600
You are given your own parish within a

186
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,480
few years.

187
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:19,520
It is a small church in a fading little

188
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:22,120
town.

189
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:23,760
The roof leaks when it rains. The boiler

190
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:26,080
is older than you are.

191
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:28,080
The congregation is mostly elderly and

192
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:30,880
shrinking every year.

193
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:32,600
You say mass every single day, sometimes

194
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:34,000
to a dozen people.

195
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,320
You hear confessions on Saturday

196
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,880
afternoons.

197
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:39,040
People tell you things they have never

198
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:43,080
told another living soul.

199
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:44,440
Affairs, thefts, hatreds, doubts, and

200
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:46,480
despair.

201
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:48,000
You carry all of it, and you can never

202
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:51,000
repeat a word.

203
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,400
The seal of confession is absolute.

204
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,040
You would go to prison before you would

205
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:56,680
ever break it.

206
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:58,680
You baptize babies and marry couples and

207
00:06:56,680 --> 00:07:00,360
bury their grandparents.

208
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:02,240
You watch whole families move through

209
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:03,800
the cycle of life.

210
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:05,520
You become the keeper of the town's

211
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,480
private history.

212
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:09,320
You are called at 3:00 in the morning to

213
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:11,000
anoint the dying.

214
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:13,080
You drive through storms to reach a

215
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,120
hospital bed in time.

216
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:16,840
You run the finances of the parish with

217
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:18,440
almost no money.

218
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:20,360
You fix the heater yourself when you

219
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:21,840
cannot afford a plumber.

220
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:24,120
You count the collection on Sunday

221
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:26,000
nights at the kitchen table.

222
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:27,480
Your father dies during your fourth year

223
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,840
as a pastor.

224
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:30,120
You say the funeral mass for him

225
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:32,560
yourself.

226
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:34,360
Your voice breaks only once during the

227
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:36,240
final blessing.

228
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:37,680
Your mother moves into a small apartment

229
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:40,040
near your rectory.

230
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:42,120
She cooks for you on Sundays and worries

231
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:44,280
that you are too thin.

232
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,960
Maria has two children now and lives

233
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,840
three towns over.

234
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:49,200
You baptized both of them with your own

235
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:52,120
hands.

236
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:55,240
The rectory bed is cold. The nights are

237
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:57,120
lonely. The silence is total.

238
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:59,280
You learn to love it.

239
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:01,800
You live inside prayer.

240
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:04,120
Sunday holds the week together.

241
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:06,840
The church fills and empties.

242
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:08,280
You shake every hand. You remember every

243
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:10,520
sorrow.

244
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:12,960
A young couple loses a baby.

245
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:15,960
You sit with them. You have no useful

246
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:19,560
words. So, you simply stay.

247
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:21,960
That is the whole job. You show up.

248
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:24,520
Christmas is the loneliest night.

249
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:26,080
You dine with mother and Maria. Then you

250
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:28,280
go back alone.

251
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:30,200
You light the candles yourself.

252
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:32,039
No one sees you do it.

253
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:33,680
That is enough for you.

254
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:35,440
You are happy in a way you did not

255
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:37,240
expect to be.

256
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:39,599
But the bishop has begun to notice how

257
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:42,320
well you run things.

258
00:08:39,599 --> 00:08:43,960
Level four, the Monsignor.

259
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:45,480
The bishop calls you to his office one

260
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:47,240
quiet afternoon.

261
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:48,920
He tells you that you have a rare gift

262
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:50,640
for administration.

263
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:52,200
He wants to send you to Rome to study

264
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:53,520
canon law.

265
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:55,000
You leave your little parish with a

266
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,560
heavy heart.

267
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,440
The parishioners throw you a farewell

268
00:08:56,560 --> 00:09:00,240
dinner and cry.

269
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:01,520
You arrive in Rome for the first time in

270
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:03,480
your life.

271
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:05,080
The city overwhelms you with its noise

272
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:07,000
and its beauty.

273
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:08,960
You study at a pontifical university

274
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,120
near the Vatican walls.

275
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:13,080
Canon law is the legal code that governs

276
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,280
the entire church.

277
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:17,600
You learn how marriages are annulled and

278
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:19,400
how disputes are judged.

279
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,839
You learn how bishops are disciplined

280
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:23,720
and how priests are removed.

281
00:09:21,839 --> 00:09:25,280
You earn your doctorate after years of

282
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:27,200
difficult work.

283
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:28,800
You are awarded the title of Monsignor

284
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,240
for your service.

285
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:32,640
It comes with purple trim on your

286
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:34,520
cassock and little else.

287
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:36,520
You return home and work inside the

288
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:38,920
diocesan offices.

289
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:40,880
You manage tribunals and review cases

290
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:42,520
and advise the bishop.

291
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:44,320
You handle the problems that nobody

292
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:47,160
wants to talk about.

293
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:48,800
A priest accused of misconduct, a parish

294
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:50,360
drowning in debt,

295
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,920
a scandal that must be contained

296
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,520
quietly.

297
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,360
You learn that the church is also a

298
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:57,240
human institution.

299
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:58,720
It is full of saints and it is full of

300
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:00,600
sinners.

301
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:02,880
You see things that test your faith more

302
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:05,000
than any book ever could.

303
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:07,440
You keep your faith anyway because the

304
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:09,520
alternative is despair.

305
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:11,520
Your mother is in her 70s now.

306
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:13,200
Her hands shake and her memory slips a

307
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:15,120
little each year.

308
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:16,720
You visit her every week and read to her

309
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:18,600
from the Psalms.

310
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:20,520
She still introduces you to strangers as

311
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:23,240
her son the priest.

312
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:25,680
Rome is stone and gold.

313
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:27,760
Every street holds centuries.

314
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:30,360
You walk where saints walked.

315
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:31,920
You pray at the apostles' tombs.

316
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:34,240
It humbles you.

317
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:35,560
Your Italian improves. Your Latin

318
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:37,560
sharpens.

319
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:39,560
You study past midnight.

320
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:42,080
Your classmates are ambitious.

321
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:43,960
Some want power, not God.

322
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:45,920
You see it in their eyes.

323
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:47,600
You swear you are different.

324
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:49,520
You hope it holds.

325
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:51,640
You miss your old parish.

326
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:53,400
You miss the leaking roof.

327
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:55,560
You did not expect that.

328
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:58,360
A parish is a home.

329
00:10:55,560 --> 00:11:00,480
Rome is grander, but colder.

330
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:02,160
Grandeur has a price.

331
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:03,960
You are climbing now, whether you ever

332
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:05,440
wanted to or not.

333
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,960
The Vatican has begun to learn your

334
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:09,400
name.

335
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:10,960
Level five, the bishop.

336
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:13,280
The letter arrives from the apostolic

337
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:15,280
nuncio in Rome. The Holy Father has

338
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:17,120
appointed you a bishop.

339
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:18,200
You read it three times before you can

340
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,839
believe it.

341
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,480
You are ordained in a ceremony that

342
00:11:19,839 --> 00:11:23,000
lasts for hours.

343
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:24,520
Three bishops lay their hands on your

344
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,480
head in succession.

345
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:28,920
You receive a ring, a staff, and a tall

346
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:30,880
pointed miter.

347
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:32,240
You are now a successor to the apostles

348
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:33,920
themselves.

349
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:36,680
You are given a diocese of your own to

350
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:38,960
shepherd. It contains a hundred parishes

351
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:41,040
and hundreds of thousands of souls.

352
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:42,160
You are responsible for every single one

353
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:44,120
of them.

354
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,560
You ordain new priests the way you were

355
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:47,560
once ordained.

356
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:49,160
You feel the strange weight of being on

357
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:51,240
the other side.

358
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,440
You confirm thousands of teenagers every

359
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:54,320
spring.

360
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,560
You travel constantly from one parish to

361
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:57,280
the next.

362
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:58,480
You manage budgets that run into the

363
00:11:57,280 --> 00:12:00,120
millions.

364
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:01,480
You close churches that can no longer

365
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:03,560
survive.

366
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:05,280
Each closing feels like a small and

367
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:06,480
personal death.

368
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:09,840
You deal with priests who are

369
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:11,880
struggling, failing, or worse.

370
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:13,920
You must investigate accusations and

371
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:15,880
make terrible decisions.

372
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,320
You sit across from victims and listen

373
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:19,400
to their pain.

374
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:22,120
You learn that leadership means carrying

375
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:23,520
burdens that crush ordinary men.

376
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:25,160
You attend conferences with other

377
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:27,080
bishops in the capital.

378
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:29,640
You learn the politics of the church,

379
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:31,680
which are real and sharp.

380
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:34,000
Some bishops are holy.

381
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:36,800
Some bishops are ambitious.

382
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:38,800
Some of them are both things at once.

383
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:40,480
You watch how they maneuver for position

384
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:42,040
and influence.

385
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:43,800
Your mother passes away during your

386
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:45,920
third year as bishop.

387
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:47,280
She dies in her sleep with her rosary in

388
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:48,640
her hand.

389
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:51,280
You say her funeral mass in the

390
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:53,480
cathedral wearing your miter.

391
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:55,040
The whole village comes. The same

392
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:56,400
village where the bell once measured

393
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,240
your days.

394
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:00,000
You bury her next to your father in the

395
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:02,440
old churchyard.

396
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Maria stands beside you, gray now

397
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:07,600
herself, holding your arm.

398
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,680
They call you Excellency.

399
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:11,800
You never get used to it.

400
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:13,760
You wear a ring of office.

401
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:15,880
People line up to kiss it.

402
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:18,040
You bless great crowds.

403
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:20,520
The gestures feel borrowed.

404
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:22,800
Then they become yours.

405
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:24,680
Your calendar fills a year out. You

406
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:27,000
sleep 5 hours.

407
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:29,400
You eat in moving cars.

408
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:32,040
Free days disappear.

409
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:34,840
A young priest weeps to you. He wants to

410
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:36,480
leave. He has fallen in love.

411
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:38,600
You do not shame him.

412
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:40,640
You remember your own vow.

413
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:42,920
You let him go gently.

414
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:45,360
You pray for him for years.

415
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:47,720
You know his pain too well.

416
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:49,840
Your vow still costs you.

417
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:51,680
You realize you are alone in a way you

418
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:54,200
never were before.

419
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:56,600
The church is your family. You remind

420
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:59,480
yourself once again.

421
00:13:56,600 --> 00:14:01,400
Level six, the archbishop.

422
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:02,960
Rome promotes you once again.

423
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,960
You are made the archbishop of a major

424
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:05,840
city.

425
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:07,720
An archdiocese is larger and more

426
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,640
important than a diocese.

427
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,080
You wear a special band of white wool

428
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:13,200
called a pallium.

429
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:14,240
The Pope blesses it himself and sends it

430
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,880
to you.

431
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:18,400
You now oversee not just your own

432
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:19,840
territory, but a whole region.

433
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:22,120
Other bishops look to you as their

434
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:24,000
senior. You sit on national committees

435
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:25,640
that shape church policy.

436
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:28,320
You speak to the press, which is

437
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:30,280
dangerous and necessary.

438
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:31,560
Every word you say can become a headline

439
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:33,080
overnight.

440
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:35,640
You learn to choose your words like a

441
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:37,200
man walking on thin ice.

442
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:39,000
You meet with politicians and business

443
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:40,560
leaders and ambassadors.

444
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,640
You advocate for the poor, the

445
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:44,200
immigrant, and the forgotten.

446
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:45,520
You also defend the church against its

447
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:47,240
many critics.

448
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:48,320
Some of those critics are right, and you

449
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:50,040
know it.

450
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:52,280
You travel to Rome several times a year

451
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:53,960
now. You begin to know the corridors of

452
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:55,520
the Vatican by heart.

453
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:57,320
You meet the cardinals who run the great

454
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:59,520
departments of the church.

455
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:01,400
You learn who holds real power and who

456
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,880
only pretends to.

457
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:04,440
You attend audiences with the Holy

458
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:06,560
Father himself.

459
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:07,960
He is old and frail, but his eyes are

460
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:09,920
still sharp.

461
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:11,320
He remembers your name and asks about

462
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:13,600
your region.

463
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:15,680
You realize that he is watching you.

464
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:17,320
The most powerful man in your world has

465
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:19,600
taken notice of you.

466
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:21,560
You return home and tell no one, but you

467
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:23,560
cannot sleep.

468
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:25,400
Maria calls you on the phone and teases

469
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:27,200
you about becoming famous.

470
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:28,880
You laugh, but you both know that

471
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:30,680
something is changing.

472
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,960
Her children are grown now with children

473
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:34,120
of their own.

474
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:36,720
Cameras follow you everywhere.

475
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:38,880
One wrong sentence ruins years.

476
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:41,160
You speak in careful circles.

477
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:43,720
You learn what not to say.

478
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:44,720
The press wants scandal. You refuse to

479
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:47,560
give it.

480
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:49,520
You meet a president. You meet a beggar.

481
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:51,720
You try to treat them the same.

482
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:53,680
It is harder than it sounds.

483
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:55,800
Power bends everyone.

484
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:57,760
You feel it bending you.

485
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:59,880
You fight it with confession.

486
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:02,080
You confess to a simple monk.

487
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,640
He shows you no deference. You are

488
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:05,720
grateful for that.

489
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:07,520
You need to be seen as a man.

490
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:09,520
Just a man.

491
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:11,560
Maria reminds you of that.

492
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:13,080
You baptize that whole family across the

493
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:14,840
long years.

494
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:16,680
You are the single thread that runs

495
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:19,520
through all of them.

496
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:21,360
Level seven, the cardinal.

497
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,360
The announcement comes from Rome at

498
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:24,560
noon.

499
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:25,960
The Holy Father has named you a cardinal

500
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,680
of the church.

501
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:30,200
You will receive the red hat in a

502
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:32,240
ceremony called a consistory.

503
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:34,640
The red symbolizes your willingness to

504
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:36,560
shed blood for the faith.

505
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:37,600
You travel to Rome and kneel before the

506
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:39,680
Pope.

507
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:40,640
He places the scarlet biretta upon your

508
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:43,720
head.

509
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:46,040
You are now a prince of the church.

510
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:47,760
You are one of roughly 200 such men in

511
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:49,760
the entire world.

512
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:51,200
You are given a titular church in Rome

513
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:53,240
as your own.

514
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:54,600
Your name is added to the college of

515
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:56,560
cardinals.

516
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:59,000
You wear scarlet robes that announce

517
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:01,120
your rank across any room.

518
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,240
People kiss your ring now, even old

519
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:04,160
friends.

520
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:05,160
It makes you uncomfortable, but you let

521
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,760
them.

522
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:09,360
You are assigned to several Vatican

523
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:11,439
departments called dicasteries.

524
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,520
You fly to Rome for meetings every few

525
00:17:11,439 --> 00:17:14,640
weeks.

526
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:16,839
You help govern the universal church,

527
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:18,600
not just one region.

528
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:20,600
You vote on matters affect more than a

529
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:22,360
billion Catholics.

530
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:23,760
You learn the deepest politics of the

531
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:25,839
Vatican now.

532
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:27,240
Alliances form and dissolve over

533
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:29,680
decades.

534
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:31,720
Old rivalries simmer beneath polite and

535
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:33,320
patient smiles.

536
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,640
You learn to read a room full of

537
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:36,560
Cardinals.

538
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:37,920
You learn who can be trusted and who

539
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:40,440
cannot.

540
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:42,760
You learn that holiness and ambition can

541
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:44,960
live in the same heart.

542
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:47,360
You examine your own heart and do not

543
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:49,240
always like what you find.

544
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:50,520
You begin to understand a terrible

545
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:53,560
truth.

546
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:55,360
One day, this Pope will die.

547
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:57,360
And the men in these red robes will

548
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:59,560
choose his successor.

549
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:01,360
You might be in that room.

550
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:02,880
You might even be considered for the

551
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:05,240
throne.

552
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:07,520
You push the thought away as pride,

553
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:09,800
but it always returns.

554
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:11,400
Maria is a great-grandmother now and

555
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:14,240
slowing down.

556
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:16,040
The robes are red as blood.

557
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:20,200
They are a warning to you.

558
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:22,560
Red for the martyrs. Red for the cost.

559
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:23,920
You dine with the Cardinals. Some are

560
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:26,480
humble men.

561
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:28,560
Some are hungry for more.

562
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:31,360
You tell them apart fast.

563
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:33,680
You learn whose smiles are real.

564
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:35,800
Rome runs on patience.

565
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:38,040
Nothing here moves fast.

566
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:40,000
Centuries are the measure.

567
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:42,160
You think that way now.

568
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,760
Your village feels distant.

569
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:46,720
The old bell is far away.

570
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:48,240
Would that boy know you?

571
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:50,400
You are not sure.

572
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:52,840
The thought sits heavy.

573
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:55,680
You pray and release it.

574
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:57,800
You call her every Sunday from Rome.

575
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:59,920
She is the last person alive who knew

576
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:02,400
you as a boy.

577
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:04,800
Level eight, the Curia Cardinal.

578
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:06,600
The Pope calls you to Rome permanently.

579
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:08,720
He needs you to run one of the great

580
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:10,360
offices of the church. Perhaps you

581
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:11,680
become the prefect of a powerful

582
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:13,200
dicastery.

583
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,840
Perhaps you become the Secretary of

584
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:16,520
State himself.

585
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:18,840
The Secretary of State is the second

586
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:20,280
most powerful man in the Vatican.

587
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,760
You move into an apartment within the

588
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,720
Vatican walls.

589
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:24,840
You now live inside the smallest country

590
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,800
on Earth.

591
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:28,280
It is barely 100 acres surrounded by the

592
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:30,080
city of Rome.

593
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:32,280
It has its own post office, its own

594
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:34,160
bank, and its own guards.

595
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:35,600
The Swiss Guard in their striped uniform

596
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:37,600
salute you.

597
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:39,120
You walk past St. Peter's Basilica every

598
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:40,520
single morning.

599
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:42,400
You attend meetings where the future of

600
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:44,040
the church is decided.

601
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,800
You manage relationships with nations

602
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:47,560
all around the world.

603
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:49,400
The Vatican has diplomatic ties with

604
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:51,040
almost every country.

605
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,840
You negotiate with presidents and prime

606
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:54,520
ministers and kings.

607
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,800
You handle crises that never reach the

608
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:57,480
newspapers.

609
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,480
A persecuted bishop in a hostile

610
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:00,280
country.

611
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:01,520
A financial scandal that must be quietly

612
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:03,160
cleaned up.

613
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:04,760
A doctrinal dispute that could split the

614
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:06,280
faithful in two.

615
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:08,520
You see the machinery behind the curtain

616
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:11,640
at last. You see the money, the

617
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:13,520
influence, and the ancient bureaucracy.

618
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:15,320
You see good men trying to do right in

619
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:16,960
an impossible system.

620
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:18,880
You see other men using the robes for

621
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:20,480
power and comfort.

622
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:22,240
You learn to govern with a patience that

623
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:24,200
spans centuries.

624
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:26,240
The church thinks in hundreds of years,

625
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:28,760
not in news cycles.

626
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:30,440
You advise the Holy Father directly now.

627
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:31,520
You sit beside him at the most important

628
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:33,680
moments.

629
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:35,480
You watch his health begin to fail.

630
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:36,640
You watch him grow tired and gray and

631
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:38,400
slow.

632
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:40,160
You know what is coming, and so does

633
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:41,680
everyone around you.

634
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:43,320
The whispering has already begun in the

635
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:45,760
quiet corridors.

636
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:48,160
Some of those whispers are about you.

637
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:50,000
Maria dies that winter. The last of your

638
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:51,920
blood from the old village.

639
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,680
You fly home to bury her, the final

640
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:56,120
funeral of your family.

641
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:57,520
The Vatican is a tiny country. It has

642
00:20:56,120 --> 00:21:00,080
its own laws.

643
00:20:57,520 --> 00:21:01,320
Much of it is ordinary, tired men buried

644
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:02,840
in paper.

645
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:05,000
Much of it is holy.

646
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:06,720
Saints knelt in its chapels.

647
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,960
You hold both truths.

648
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:11,600
The Holy Father trusts you. That trust

649
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:14,280
is heavy. You guard it carefully.

650
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:16,560
You join the hardest talks, wars,

651
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:19,080
famines, persecution.

652
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:21,640
You carry unseen burdens. You share them

653
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:23,040
with no one. You have no wife. You have

654
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:25,000
no child.

655
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:27,680
Only God hears the weight.

656
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:30,080
You are 68 now. Your knees ache on the

657
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:31,640
marble. You kneel anyway.

658
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:33,880
You stand alone at the grave where your

659
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:35,880
mother and father already lie.

660
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:38,280
You are the last one left now, and the

661
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:40,920
village bell still rings.

662
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:42,960
Level nine, the papabile.

663
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:44,200
The Holy Father dies on a quiet morning

664
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:46,120
in spring.

665
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:47,880
The bells of Rome toll the news across

666
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:49,800
the entire world.

667
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:51,560
As a senior cardinal, you help manage

668
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:54,120
the days that follow.

669
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:56,800
You are now what they call a papabile. A

670
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:58,320
man who could be pope.

671
00:21:56,800 --> 00:22:01,280
The church enters the period called the

672
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:03,080
sede vacante, the empty seat.

673
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:05,120
The camerlengo confirms the death and

674
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:06,880
seals the papal apartments.

675
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:08,800
The funeral draws millions of mourners

676
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:10,480
to St. Peter's Square.

677
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:12,280
You can celebrate the mass before the

678
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:14,920
eyes of the whole world.

679
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:16,280
Then, the doors close, and the real work

680
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:18,320
begins.

681
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:20,040
The cardinals under 80 gather from every

682
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:22,520
corner of the earth.

683
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:24,280
There are about 120 of you.

684
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:26,200
You are locked inside the Vatican until

685
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:29,360
a decision is made.

686
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:31,560
The word conclave means with a key.

687
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:33,680
You are sworn to absolute secrecy under

688
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:35,600
pain of excommunication.

689
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:37,520
You file into the Sistine Chapel beneath

690
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:39,680
Michelangelo's ceiling.

691
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:41,120
The Last Judgment looms over the altar

692
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:42,640
before you.

693
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:44,080
You take your oath with your hand upon

694
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:46,280
the Gospels.

695
00:22:44,080 --> 00:22:48,160
Then, the master of ceremonies cries out

696
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:49,960
the ancient command.

697
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:51,680
Everyone who is not a cardinal must

698
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:53,560
leave the chapel.

699
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:54,880
The great doors are shut and bolted from

700
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:57,200
within.

701
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:58,760
You vote in silence, writing a name on a

702
00:22:57,200 --> 00:23:00,520
folded ballot.

703
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:02,120
You walk it to the altar and swear

704
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:03,560
before God.

705
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:05,040
The ballots are counted aloud in the

706
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:06,840
heavy hush.

707
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:08,280
No one reaches the two-thirds needed on

708
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:10,240
the first day.

709
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:12,240
The ballots are burned and black smoke

710
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:15,160
rises over the square.

711
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:17,600
The crowd outside groans and waits.

712
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:18,960
Night falls and you cannot sleep.

713
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:20,760
You pray harder than you have ever

714
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:22,400
prayed in your life.

715
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:24,200
You feel the votes beginning to gather

716
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:26,840
around your own name.

717
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:27,800
You are terrified by it. You do not want

718
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:30,160
it.

719
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:31,920
And yet, you cannot refuse what God may

720
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:33,600
be asking of you.

721
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:35,480
The next morning, the voting resumes

722
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:37,560
beneath the painted saints.

723
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:39,360
Round after round, your name climbs

724
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:41,840
higher and higher.

725
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:44,560
The world watches a chimney.

726
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:47,480
Black smoke means not yet.

727
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:49,240
White smoke means a father.

728
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:51,600
You watch from inside.

729
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:54,080
You know what they do not.

730
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:56,480
You know whose name rises.

731
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:58,200
More and more, it is yours.

732
00:23:56,480 --> 00:24:00,120
Your hands are cold.

733
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:02,360
You did not ask for this.

734
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:04,680
No honest man does.

735
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:05,880
The throne is a cross. Everyone here

736
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:08,040
knows it.

737
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:09,400
You look up at the ceiling. Adam reaches

738
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:12,640
for God.

739
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:14,160
You feel small. You always have.

740
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:16,040
Maybe that is why.

741
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:18,240
Or you will soon learn.

742
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:19,640
You bow your head. You wait for the will

743
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:21,240
of God.

744
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:22,760
You feel the eyes of the other cardinals

745
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:24,960
turning toward you.

746
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:26,680
The weight of 2,000 years settles onto

747
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:29,840
your shoulders.

748
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:32,240
Level 10, the Supreme Pontiff.

749
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:34,280
The final ballot is counted. Your name

750
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:36,320
is read aloud and the chapel falls

751
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:38,560
completely silent.

752
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:41,040
The Dean of the college turns to you and

753
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:43,160
asks the ancient question.

754
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:44,840
Do you accept your election as Supreme

755
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:47,240
Pontiff?

756
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:49,400
Every man who ever sat on this throne

757
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:52,240
had to answer in this same trembling

758
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:54,560
moment. You think of the village bell,

759
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:58,520
your mother's rosary, your father's

760
00:24:54,560 --> 00:25:01,080
silent prayers, and the long road here.

761
00:24:58,520 --> 00:25:03,080
You whisper a single word.

762
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:05,200
I accept.

763
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:07,240
They ask what name you will take, and

764
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:08,640
you choose a saint you have loved since

765
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:10,680
boyhood.

766
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:12,920
The cardinals approach one by one to

767
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:14,800
pledge their obedience to you.

768
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:16,280
You are no longer the man you were an

769
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:18,680
hour ago.

770
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:21,520
You are dressed in white in a small room

771
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:25,600
they call the Room of Tears.

772
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:27,200
Now, at last, you understand the name.

773
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:29,680
The senior cardinal steps onto the

774
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:31,560
balcony above St. Peter's Square.

775
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:33,000
He proclaims the ancient words to the

776
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:34,960
waiting world.

777
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:36,880
Habemus papam.

778
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:39,160
We have a pope.

779
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:41,080
A hundred thousand people roar up out of

780
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:43,640
the darkness below.

781
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:45,800
Then you walk out onto that balcony, and

782
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:48,080
the roar becomes a wall of sound you

783
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:50,680
feel in your chest.

784
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:52,280
You raise your hand and bless the city

785
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:55,040
and the world.

786
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:57,520
You are now the spiritual father of more

787
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:59,440
than a billion souls.

788
00:25:57,520 --> 00:26:02,560
You are the Bishop of Rome, the

789
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:03,840
successor of Peter, the Vicar of Christ

790
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:06,480
on Earth.

791
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:08,960
You hold a power that no army and no

792
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:12,480
fortune can ever match.

793
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:14,840
And yet, you have never felt so small.

794
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:16,600
You move into the papal apartments, or

795
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:18,240
perhaps you refuse them and stay

796
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:20,400
somewhere simpler.

797
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:23,480
The whole world watches every word you

798
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:25,640
speak and every gesture you make.

799
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:27,520
You meet kings and presidents who come

800
00:26:25,640 --> 00:26:29,600
to kiss your ring.

801
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:32,440
You wash the feet of prisoners and

802
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:35,320
embrace the sick and the dying.

803
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:38,560
You carry the scandals of 2,000 years

804
00:26:35,320 --> 00:26:40,480
and the hopes of the living all at once.

805
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:42,480
You sign documents that will guide the

806
00:26:40,480 --> 00:26:43,880
faith for generations after you are

807
00:26:42,480 --> 00:26:46,360
gone.

808
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:49,000
You are never alone, and yet you are

809
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:51,080
lonelier than you have ever been.

810
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:55,160
There is no one above you now to confess

811
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:58,040
your own doubts to, except God himself.

812
00:26:55,160 --> 00:27:00,360
You are 75 years old and the boy from

813
00:26:58,040 --> 00:27:02,240
the mountain village has reached the top

814
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:04,680
of the world.

815
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:05,720
You think of Maria, of your mother and

816
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:07,800
father,

817
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:09,280
and of the old pastor who first believed

818
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:12,440
in you.

819
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:14,240
None of them lived to see this day.

820
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:16,120
You pray for them every night in your

821
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:18,760
private chapel.

822
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:22,000
You are the last of your family now.

823
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:23,920
You carry their memory like a candle.

824
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:26,400
And you carry a secret that you can

825
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:28,560
share with no one.

826
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:30,920
You are afraid.

827
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:33,400
You are afraid because you know that you

828
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:35,400
are only a man.

829
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:37,040
You know that the white robes do not

830
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:38,920
make you holy.

831
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:41,880
You know that millions will look to you

832
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:44,200
for answers you do not have.

833
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:46,240
You know your every failure will be

834
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,840
written into the history of the church

835
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:50,240
forever.

836
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:52,640
You know that one careless word could

837
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:54,080
wound the faith of millions across the

838
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:56,480
world.

839
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:59,240
You know that history will judge you

840
00:27:56,480 --> 00:28:01,240
long after you are dust.

841
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:04,800
So you kneel in silence before the

842
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:06,680
altar, an old man in white.

843
00:28:04,800 --> 00:28:09,840
You ask for the strength to carry a

844
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:11,520
weight no human shoulder was ever built

845
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:13,840
to bear.

846
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:15,440
The bells of Rome ring out across the

847
00:28:13,840 --> 00:28:18,040
seven hills.

848
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:21,080
They are ringing for you now.

849
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:23,520
You think of a smaller bell long ago in

850
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:26,160
a poor mountain village.

851
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:28,080
The same bell once called a barefoot boy

852
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:30,120
to morning mass.

853
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:31,600
That boy could never have dreamed of

854
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:34,840
this.

855
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:37,160
Neither could the old man he became.

856
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:39,040
Somewhere in a village in the mountains,

857
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:40,560
a church bell is ringing across the

858
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:43,160
rooftops.

859
00:28:40,560 --> 00:28:45,520
A small boy sits in an empty pew

860
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:47,920
breathing in the incense.

861
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:50,200
